{"unit":4,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 4","tracks":{"a43":"Track_4.3.mp3"},"SEGS":{"prog":["a43",3.79,null]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 4 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Places and predictions</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 4, with four questions that come back from Units 1&ndash;3. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u4\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">The path was so&hellip; that we had to stop every few minutes.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">communal</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">steep</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">permanent</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">A thirty-minute ferry connects the island to the&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">suburb</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">valley</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">mainland</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">The village is two hours from the nearest shop &mdash; it really is&hellip;\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">miles from anywhere</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">packed like sardines</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">neat and tidy</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">Factories in the valley&hellip; smoke all day.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">run out of</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">give off</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">get rid of</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match the two halves of each phrase. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"p1\">settle</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"p2\">set</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"p3\">make</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"p4\">feel</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"p5\">run</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"p4\" data-short=\"at home\">at home</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"p1\" data-short=\"down\">down</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"p5\" data-short=\"out of space\">out of space</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"p3\" data-short=\"room\">room</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"p2\" data-short=\"off early\">off early</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with one word from the box: <b>available &middot; include &middot; per</b>.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\">Could you tell me whether any rooms are still <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"available\" data-why=\"<b>Available</b> = there are still some free.\"> in July?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\">Does that price <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"include\" data-why=\"<b>Include</b> = have inside the price.\"> breakfast?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">The course costs ninety euros <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"per\" data-why=\"<b>Per</b> week = for each week.\"> week.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">Look at those clouds. It&hellip; rain.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">will</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">may</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">is going to</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">That is the doorbell. I&hellip; it.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">will get</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">am going to get</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">get</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">By 2050, roughly two thirds of the world&rsquo;s population&hellip; in cities.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">are living</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">will live</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">live</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">Prices in the suburbs&hellip; to rise for the next few years.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">will likely</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">may be likely</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">are likely</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">How certain is the speaker? Choose.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">The trend will definitely spread around the world. <select data-answer=\"1\" data-why=\"<b>certain</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"2\">very probable</option><option value=\"1\">certain</option><option value=\"3\">only possible</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">Ninety-two per cent of the population is likely to live in cities. <select data-answer=\"2\" data-why=\"<b>very probable</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"2\">very probable</option><option value=\"3\">only possible</option><option value=\"1\">certain</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">A walk in the forest might prevent you from becoming ill. <select data-answer=\"3\" data-why=\"<b>only possible</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"2\">very probable</option><option value=\"1\">certain</option><option value=\"3\">only possible</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the words in brackets into the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>not / be</i>) Don&rsquo;t worry &mdash; I promise I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"won't be|will not be\" data-why=\"A promise at the moment of speaking &rarr; <b>will</b>.\"> late.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>study</i>) She has already chosen the university. She <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"is going to study|'s going to study\" data-why=\"A decision already made &rarr; <b>be going to</b>.\"> architecture.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>probably / not / happen</i>) It <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"probably won't happen|probably will not happen\" data-why=\"In a negative, <i>probably</i> comes <b>before</b> <i>won&rsquo;t</i>.\"> before 2040.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">The ferry service <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"will probably be\" data-why=\"In a positive sentence <i>probably</i> goes <b>after</b> <i>will</i>: <i>will probably be</i>.\"> busy on Sunday.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">The cost of building <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"is likely to rise\" data-why=\"<b>Be likely to</b> + base verb: <i>is likely to rise</i>.\"> again.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">Perhaps the company will build on the water. <i>(may)</i><br>The company <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"may build on the water\" data-why=\"<b>May</b> + base verb for a possibility.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">I have decided to move to Amsterdam next year. <i>(going to)</i><br>I <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"am going to move to amsterdam next year|'m going to move to amsterdam next year\" data-why=\"A plan already decided &rarr; <b>be going to</b>.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The city that is moving</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">Jakarta is sinking faster than almost any large city on earth. Indonesia&rsquo;s answer is not to defend it, but to leave.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>Parts of northern Jakarta have dropped by more than two and a half metres since the 1970s. The reason is not only the ocean. The city has run out of piped water in many districts, so households and factories pump it out of the ground beneath them, and the land settles into the space they leave. A sea wall now stands higher than the roofs behind it.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>In 2019 the government announced that the capital would move to a site on the island of Borneo, more than a thousand kilometres inland. The new city, Nusantara, is being built in what was recently forest. Officials say the first civil servants are going to settle there within a few years and that the population is likely to reach nearly two million by 2045.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>Not everybody is convinced. Moving a capital is one of the most expensive things a state can do, and similar projects elsewhere have taken far longer than promised. Environmental groups point out that the site is home to species that live nowhere else, and that a city built in a forest may simply move the damage rather than avoid it. There is also a plainer objection: Jakarta will still be there, with ten million people in it, whatever happens on Borneo.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>Planners answer that the two problems are separate. Nusantara is meant to take the pressure off, not to replace what exists; Jakarta will remain the country&rsquo;s business centre, and the pumping restrictions and the sea defences are going ahead anyway. Whether the new capital will work is a question nobody can answer for twenty years. What is certain is that other coastal cities are watching closely, because a great many of them have the same problem and no forest to move into.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">The main reason northern Jakarta is sinking is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">the weight of new buildings</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">water being pumped out from under the city</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">the sea wall being built too high</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">According to paragraph D, what will happen to Jakarta?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">it will be closed and emptied</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">it will become a national park</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">it will stay, and stay the business centre</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">The new capital is being built on the coast. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: the site is more than a thousand kilometres <b>False</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">Environmental groups are worried about the wildlife at the new site. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph C: species that live nowhere else.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">The move has already cost more than the government expected. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"The text says such projects are expensive, but never gives the actual cost.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">The government made the announcement in 2019. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph B says so directly.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph C, <i>a plainer objection</i> introduces an argument that is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">simpler and harder to answer than the others</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">less important than the others</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">made only by environmental groups</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">The last sentence suggests that other coastal cities\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">have already begun moving their capitals</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">think Jakarta has solved the problem</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">face the same danger with fewer options</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play the recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('prog',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Science Matters &middot; the whole programme\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 4.3</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">How certain is Julie about each of these? Listen for the exact word she uses.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">that screen use will spread around the world <select data-answer=\"1\" data-why=\"She says it <b>certain</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"2\">very probable</option><option value=\"3\">only possible</option><option value=\"1\">certain</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">that forest bathing prevents illness <select data-answer=\"3\" data-why=\"She says it <b>only possible</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"3\">only possible</option><option value=\"2\">very probable</option><option value=\"1\">certain</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">that Finland will open its own centres <select data-answer=\"3\" data-why=\"She says Finland <b>only possible</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"1\">certain</option><option value=\"3\">only possible</option><option value=\"2\">very probable</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">When the presenter says &ldquo;Really? That seems very hard to believe&rdquo;, he is\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">bored</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">sceptical</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">angry</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">Why does Julie mention teenagers in California?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">to show that American teenagers are unusual</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">to explain why parks cost money</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">to show that living near a park changes how active people are</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">The purpose of the whole programme is to\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">ask why people go outside less, and whether it matters</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">advertise forest bathing holidays</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">compare the climates of Japan and Britain</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the version you would actually write to a company.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\"><select data-answer=\"Could you tell me whether any places are still available?\" data-why=\"After <i>Could you tell me whether any places are still available?</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Are there any places still available?</option><option>Could you tell me whether any places are still available?</option><option>Could you tell me are there any places available?</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\"><select data-answer=\"I would be grateful if you could confirm the total cost.\" data-why=\"<b>I would be grateful if you could confirm the total cost.</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>I would be grateful if you could confirm the total cost.</option><option>Tell me the total cost.</option><option>I am grateful you confirm the total cost.</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\"><select data-answer=\"Do you happen to know how many students there are in each group?\" data-why=\"<i>Do you happen to know how many students there are in each group?</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Do you happen to know how many students are there in each group?</option><option>How many students in each group?</option><option>Do you happen to know how many students there are in each group?</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Where does each line belong?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Mail\">I am writing to enquire about your summer courses.</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Chat\">Hiya, quick q &mdash; any spaces left in July?</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Mail\">Yours faithfully, Aizhan Serikova</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Chat\">Let me know! Thanks</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Mail\"><h5>The formal email</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Chat\"><h5>A message to a friend</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the four parts of the enquiry email in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"e2,e4,e1,e3\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"e1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I am attaching my most recent certificate, in case it is useful.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"e2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I am writing to enquire about the summer courses advertised on your website.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"e3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I look forward to hearing from you. Yours faithfully, Aizhan Serikova</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"e4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Could you tell me whether any places are still available in July, and what the cost per week is?</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Two of these gaps come back from earlier units. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span></p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Nurlan</b>So you have finally decided?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Yes. We <select data-answer=\"are going to move\" data-why=\"A decision already taken &rarr; <b>are going to move</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>will move</option><option>are going to move</option><option>move</option></select> out to the suburbs in September.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Nurlan</b>The rent there is climbing too, you know.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>It <select data-answer=\"is likely to\" data-why=\"Very probable &rarr; <b>is likely to</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>will likely</option><option>may to</option><option>is likely to</option></select> keep climbing everywhere. But we <select data-answer=\"will probably save\" data-why=\"In a positive sentence <i>will probably save</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>will probably save</option><option>probably will save</option><option>are probably saving</option></select> about a third.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Nurlan</b>Miles from anywhere, though.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Twenty minutes on the train. <span class=\"pill-rec\">recycled</span> I <select data-answer=\"have known\" data-why=\"A state from the past up to now &rarr; present perfect.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>am knowing</option><option>have known</option><option>know since</option></select> that line since I was at school.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Nurlan</b>And the flat here?</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>Somebody is coming to see it tomorrow. <select data-answer=\"If they like it,\" data-why=\"A real possibility &rarr; present simple after <i>If they like it,</i>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>If they will like it,</option><option>If they liked it,</option><option>If they like it,</option></select> we sign next week. <select data-answer=\"Luckily,\" data-why=\"Good news that came by chance.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Luckily,</option><option>Unfortunately,</option><option>Personally,</option></select> the landlord is being reasonable about the date.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 100&ndash;120 words. Give yourself twenty minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> You have seen an advertisement for a two-week summer course abroad. Write a formal email of enquiry. Say why you are writing in one sentence, ask two questions about places and price, ask two further questions of your own, offer something the reader has not asked for, and close properly.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"Dear Sir or Madam,   I am writing to enquire about&hellip;   Could you tell me whether&hellip;   I would also be grateful if you could&hellip;   Yours faithfully,\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your email must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li><b>Could you tell me whether&hellip;</b> with the word order back to normal</li>\n        <li><b>I would be grateful if you could&hellip;</b> and one softer question</li>\n        <li>the questions grouped so the reader can answer them one by one</li>\n        <li>the right pair: <b>Dear Sir or Madam &rarr; Yours faithfully</b></li>\n        <li>four words from this unit: <b>available, include, per, confirm, book, cost</b></li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; predict, then decide</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Describe the place where you live and say how it will be different in twenty years. Ninety seconds. <b>Part B.</b> Then answer: <i>would you live on the water, or in a city built in a forest?</i> Say what you are going to do about where you live, and what you think is only possible.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>at least three different degrees of certainty: <b>will definitely / is likely to / may / might</b></li>\n        <li>one <b>be going to</b> for something you have already decided</li>\n        <li>one <b>will</b> for a decision you make while you are speaking</li>\n        <li><i>probably</i> in the right place, in a positive and in a negative sentence</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>It will definitely&hellip; &middot; It is likely to&hellip; &middot; It may / might&hellip; &middot; It probably won&rsquo;t&hellip; &middot; I am going to&hellip; &middot; Actually, I&rsquo;ll&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my email says why I am writing before it asks anything</li>\n        <li>every question is wrapped, and the word order inside is normal</li>\n        <li>the questions are grouped, not run together in one block</li>\n        <li>my opening and my sign-off match each other</li>\n        <li>I used at least three different degrees of certainty when I spoke</li>\n        <li>I used <i>be going to</i> for a decision I had already taken</li>\n        <li>I put <i>probably</i> after <i>will</i> and before <i>won&rsquo;t</i></li>\n        <li>I spoke for ninety seconds without stopping to translate</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}